# One in-app browser tab

This repo’s agents keep spawning Cursor Browser / Simple Browser tabs (`127.0.0.1 :8080`, `Browser`) that `browser_tabs` list cannot see or close. **Never open another one.**

## Required

1. Call `cursor-ide-browser` `browser_tabs` with `action: "list"` **before** any navigate/lock/snapshot.
2. If a tab exists, reuse it: `browser_lock` on that `viewId`, then `browser_navigate` with that `viewId` only.
3. Keep **at most one** tab. When done, `browser_tabs` `close` extras from **highest index down to 1**. Leave index 0 if you still need a preview.
4. Prefer local files, `curl`, or the user’s already-open tab over opening a browser.

## Forbidden

- `newTab: true`
- `position: "active"` or `position: "side"` (unless the user explicitly asks to reveal the browser)
- `browser_tabs` `action: "new"`
- `browser_navigate` when list is empty (do **not** create a tab to “fix” an empty list)
- `cursor-app-control` `open_resource` with `http://` or `https://` URLs — the workbench opener spawns **Simple Browser** tabs MCP cannot list or close
- Opening `http://127.0.0.1:8080` (or any localhost) in Simple Browser / a new Browser view

```text
# ❌ BAD
browser_navigate url=http://127.0.0.1:8080/ newTab=true position=active
open_resource uri=http://127.0.0.1:8080/

# ✅ GOOD
browser_tabs action=list
# reuse listed viewId; if list is empty, do not open a tab — use the existing editor tab or curl
browser_navigate url=http://127.0.0.1:8080/ viewId=<existing>
```
